Hi,

First, terrific tool.

I am just starting to learn ggplot2 and grid graphics.
I am wondering if it is possible to directly plot a function without
the initial plot?

something along the lines of:

x<-seq(-3,3,.01)
ggplot() + stat_function(fun = dnorm,args=list(x=x,m=0,sd=1))

It appears that data is essential to create the plot. Putting x in a
data.frame doesnot help either.
I am sure I am missing the point here.

Thanks in advance,

